[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Patchy runs from %%RELEASE%% as the www user and needs PostgreSQL with
the citext extension, databases/postgresql18-contrib.

To set it up:

 1. Create a database and a role for it, then copy
    %%ETCDIR%%/patchy.env.sample to %%ETCDIR%%/patchy.env and set
    DATABASE_URL, SECRET_KEY_BASE, PHX_HOST and PORT in it. Keep the
    file readable by www only.

 2. Enable the service, create the tables and start it:

      service patchy enable
      service patchy migrate
      service patchy start

 3. Put a TLS proxy in front of the port that passes X-Forwarded-Proto
    and X-Forwarded-For, then register at https://PHX_HOST/users/register
    and make an API token at /settings/api for arc. The first account is
    the administrator. Later accounts wait for approval under /admin/users
    unless REQUIRE_APPROVAL=0 is set in patchy.env.

The hook that closes revisions when their commits land is at
%%RELEASE%%/lib/patchy-*/priv/scripts/patchy-post-receive and needs
ftp/curl. The README in %%DOCSDIR%% has the details.
EOM
}
]
